      "content": "That's a huge gamble. If they ask him directly, \"Did you oppose this specific bill because you thought it was fiscally irresponsible?\" and he says yes, he's basically admitting he lied about the flaws in the text. If he says no, he looks like he's dodging. Are you seriously suggesting we manufacture an \"expert analysis\" to cover up the fact that he just didn't want to vote for it? That sounds incredibly risky if it comes out that we're spinning the facts.",
